From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] unit: test the call settings requests

Run the real binder_call_settings.c, binder_call_forwarding.c and
binder_call_barring.c against an imitation of the radio service.

getCallWaiting is answered the way the MTK RIL does it and the way the
interface says, with errors, with a short response, with something
else altogether and over AIDL. Every supplementary service request is
checked for its timeout and for not being blocking. For barring, the
tests go through the sequence of queries of oFono's GetProperties: the
modem refuses, one request gets to the radio and no more after that
until the SIM, the radio state or a set changes that. What must not be
taken for a refusal (timeout, failed transaction, other errors, a
modem which has answered) leads to all the queries being sent again.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
